WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.012
Unit 2 reads the workbook chapter,

2
00:00:02.012 --> 00:00:05.725
starting with what Microsoft gives
you and what it leaves to you.

3
00:00:05.725 --> 00:00:10.937
Learn publishes one sample query per question:
all active events, health advisories,

4
00:00:10.937 --> 00:00:16.075
upcoming retirements and planned maintenance,
each returning different columns.

5
00:00:16.075 --> 00:00:20.044
The kit builds one events query from
the all-active sample, adding the

6
00:00:20.044 --> 00:00:24.500
retirement sample's event subtype and
the advisory sample's time conversion.

7
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:27.725
Learn's samples return one row
per event per subscription,

8
00:00:27.725 --> 00:00:30.950
so the same outage would be
counted once per subscription.

9
00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:34.800
The kit merges rows by
tracking I D into one notice.

10
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.916
Learn gives event types,
not what to do about them,

11
00:00:37.916 --> 00:00:40.175
so the kit maps them to the six kinds.

12
00:00:40.175 --> 00:00:45.150
Nothing says action is required, so the
kit states a rule, and the record names it.

13
00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:48.387
And for the alert policy,
Learn gives portal steps.

14
00:00:48.387 --> 00:00:52.270
The kit writes a plan file a
reviewer can approve before it runs.
